panfrost/kmod: kbase on the job manager waits for room in its table of open submissions

The tree's JM submission keeps each submission's sequence number in open_seq[256] until the event
thread has run its callback, but frees its atom numbers (at most 255 in flight) as soon as their
events come. So the submitting thread can make new submissions while finished ones still wait for
their callbacks, and more than 256 can be open: open_seq then overflows into nr_open_seq and
in_flight, the queue's counters are wrong, and a wait for idle can go on for ever. Many quick
submissions in a row make it happen.

With this patch a submission also waits until open_seq has room; the event thread already wakes it
when it removes one.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -1696,7 +1696,9 @@
       return seq;
    }
 
-   while (q->free_atoms < need)
+   /* A submission stays open until its callback has run, after its atoms are free again, so more
+    * than 255 can be open: wait for room in open_seq too, which they overflowed. */
+   while (q->free_atoms < need || q->nr_open_seq >= ARRAY_SIZE(q->open_seq))
       pthread_cond_wait(&q->cond, &q->lock);
 
 
